;; snug's version: the single source for every artefact (owner decision O2;
;; docs/release-policy.md §1.1, D343).
;;
;; :version      the version a release build stamps. `bb stamp` writes it onto
;;               every version site (both package.json files, both Cargo.toml
;;               files, host/js/src/version.mjs, kin's snug-version literal) and
;;               re-emits gen/. Changing it is part of a release commit.
;; :placeholder  what every version site holds in the tracked tree. Stamped
;;               versions are never checked in (owner, 2026-11-12): `bb stamp`
;;               runs only in a detached release worktree or an exported copy,
;;               and `bb versions` (a land and release gate) fails if any site
;;               holds anything else. It is valid semver, so the unstamped tree
;;               builds, tests and packs, and a Program it compiles says
;;               "0.0.0-unreleased" in its producer field.
;;
;; Both must be semver strings of at most 32 bytes (the Program container's
;; producer field). kin/scripts/version-sites.mjs reads this file.
{:version     "0.1.0"
 :placeholder "0.0.0-unreleased"}
